%n ibrī | kūdannu | ṭardu | akkannu | ša šadî | nimru | ša ṣēri
#note: @bib{RN117@856}: “(…) The nuances of the word @i{ṭardu} are several here. Enkidu was a famously swift runner until he was effectively banished from his homeland by the wiles of a woman. Now he is chased by death, a more lethal pursuer. He is a mule because mules, being infertile, die as he does, without offspring.”
// L I.4 SB "X" 126
// L I.4 SB "X" 226

